window.docContents[141].resolve({"/part-4-frameworks/#part-4-frameworks":{"contents":"Parts I–III focused on real numbers, subsets of \\mathbb{R}, and functions \\mathbb{R} \\to \\mathbb{R}. But modern mathematics also quantifies over topologies (sets of sets of points), measures (functions from sets of sets to \\mathbb{R}), Banach spaces and their dual spaces, Boolean algebras, and infinite graphs. How do we extend all higher-order structures over any base set X simultaneously with a single *-transform?\n\nPart IV answers this with Abraham Robinson and Elias Zakon's Superstructure Framework, constructs Enlargements via fine ultrafilters over finite subsets, and proves the equivalence between Saturation, Permanence, and Comprehensiveness.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Lectures on the Hyperreals — Interactive Lean 4 & Spatial Edition","header":"4. Part IV — Nonstandard Frameworks, Enlargements & Saturation","id":"/part-4-frameworks/#part-4-frameworks"}});